exports[`render — prompt kompilyatori > shablon: kirish turi → yorugʻlik → kontekst → material → (qoʻshimcha) → geometriya → sifat 1`] = `"Image 1 is the BASE image. INPUT: the base image is an urban master plan / city block shown as a 3D massing model (buildings, streets, trees). Turn it into a finished image. LIGHTING: warm continental summer light, light dust haze. CONTEXT: Tashkent, Uzbekistan: plane trees (chinar) and mulberry along streets, open irrigation ditches (ariq), local people, Central Asian urban context. MATERIALS: local brick, light plaster and concrete facades; use the facade and ground materials, textures and colours of image 2 (material reference). ADDITIONAL: terrakota gʻisht fasad. GEOMETRY (highest priority, overrides everything above): keep EXACTLY the same camera angle, framing, composition and perspective. Keep every building in the same position with the same footprint, height, number of floors, roof shape and window rhythm; keep the street layout and block shapes. Do not add or remove buildings. The scene contains exactly 12 buildings, 5 to 9 floors. QUALITY: photorealistic architectural visualization. High resolution, sharp details, correct perspective, no distortion. Do not add any text, labels, watermarks or borders."`;
